From 5a1579ca99e4de6a84ae4d73a5d61e905ec7a429 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:40:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/15] rdna-boosts: block 03: chunked gated-delta-net prefill

Sources: old 02 (whole block).

Fold (r91): fold every ubatch into the per-sequence rollback tracker (issue #131).
`prepare()` recorded each sequence's last-batch shape from `ubatches.back()` only, so a
sequence that ran in a non-final ubatch of a multi-ubatch call kept an older count -- typically
its own prefill chunk.  The guard then compared a rejection rollback against a completed
prefill and warned about a batch boundary that never happened (observed 4571-token case,
reproduced on gfx1201: 1 warning -> 0 with this fix).  Every ubatch is now folded in, oldest
first.  Also adds the `LLAMA_RS_ROLLBACK_DEBUG` RSPREP/RSROLL instrumentation that proved it.
Text-identical pre/post on gfx1151 and gfx1201.  Record: archive/work/rs-rollback-boundary/.

Fold (r195): a cell that find_slot moves keeps its rollback snapshot planes.  build_rs
relocates the "extra states" (the cells inside [head, head+n_rs) that no sequence of this
ubatch uses) by copying plane 0 only, so a moved cell's planes 1..n_rs_seq stay at the old
index, where the cells that take their place overwrite them -- and that sequence's next
rollback then reads another sequence's snapshot (or zeroed rows).  From 3 cells on,
find_slot's gather-and-reorder moves a live cell whenever a multi-sequence ubatch's cell range
spans a third cell, so a 3- or 4-slot server with speculative decoding hits it.  build_rs now
also copies planes 1..n_rs_seq of the extra states, gathered through a new input
`s_copy_extra` before this ubatch writes its snapshots; the source ids use `s_src()`, not
`s_copy()`, because `s_copy()` consumes the sequence's pending rollback index.  Where no extra
state exists (n_rs == n_seqs, i.e. every single-sequence batch and a 2-cell cache) the graph
does not change.  The defect is upstream's (6050b467c and master 0ec4027a2 carry the same
build_rs); both copies are in upstream/recurrent-moved-cell-snapshots/.  Contribution by
overdoingism (PR #261).  Record: archive/work/recurrent-moved-cell-snapshots/.
